+## Fresh-session recovery walkthrough
+
+Use this procedure after a session stops. A saved checkpoint is evidence to inspect.
+It is not permission to repeat an external action.
+
+1. Select the saved instance and project root. Use the same `STATEWELL_HOME`.
+   Read the repository instructions and inspect the installed `statewell --help`.
+2. Put the saved task identifier in `/tmp/task-reference.json`.
+   Use the following input structure:
+
+   ```json
+   {"taskId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"}
+   ```
+
+   Read the task context through the public command-line interface (CLI):
+
+   ```sh
+   statewell task context --instance test --root /absolute/project --input /tmp/task-reference.json
+   ```
+
+3. Compare the saved repository state with the actual files before you edit them.
+   Read the uncommitted changes and the retained check results.
+
+   ```sh
+   git status --short
+   git branch --show-current
+   git rev-parse HEAD
+   git diff -- docs/INSTANCE-CLI.md
+   ```
+
+   Inspect the actual result of each uncertain external action.
+   For example, read an existing receipt before you repeat a request.
+   A lost response does not show that an external action failed.
